{"4935000": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Infinite Elevator", "steam_appid": 4935000, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i><strong>Get to the ground floor and escape the elevator nightmare.</strong></i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Every floor opens on the same hallway. Doors, lamps. But the deeper you descend, the less you can trust it. Something may have moved. Something may be standing there. Or nothing has changed at all — doubt and fear are the only things in the corridor with you.</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <strong>Key Features</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>- 20+ anomalies, from blatant intrusions to details you'll swear were always like that</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>- Core judgment loop: same → down, different → up</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>- Failure is silent — the game never tells you when you were wrong</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>- Retro PS1-style visuals, one warm light, one hallway, one elevator</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>- Short, dense runs built for &quot;one more floor&quot;</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>-  11 languages supported</i></p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i><strong>Get to the ground floor and escape the elevator nightmare.</strong></i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Every floor opens on the same hallway. Doors, lamps. But the deeper you descend, the less you can trust it. Something may have moved. Something may be standing there. Or nothing has changed at all — doubt and fear are the only things in the corridor with you.</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > <strong>Key Features</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>- 20+ anomalies, from blatant intrusions to details you'll swear were always like that</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>- Core judgment loop: same → down, different → up</i></p><p class=\"bb_p